### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### Online Teaching Platform — manual API test script
###
### How to use:
###   1. Make sure the Django server is running: `python manage.py runserver`
###   2. Make sure the Celery worker is running: `celery -A backend worker -l info`
###   3. Click "Send Request" above each block (it appears between the lines)
###   4. Run blocks in order — later blocks reuse tokens/ids from earlier ones
###
### Tip: the `# @name xyz` comment names a request; later requests can read
### its response with {{xyz.response.body.<field>}}.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

@base = http://localhost:8000/api

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### AUTH — log in as student and as teacher
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

### Log in as student1 -> captures access token as studentLogin.response.body.access
# @name studentLogin
POST {{base}}/auth/login/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "student1",
  "password": "student123123"
}

### Log in as teacher1
# @name teacherLogin
POST {{base}}/auth/login/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "teacher1",
  "password": "teacher123"
}

### Convenience aliases — these resolve every time you send a request below
@studentToken = {{studentLogin.response.body.access}}
@teacherToken = {{teacherLogin.response.body.access}}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### USERS — current user
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

### Who am I (student)?
GET {{base}}/users/me/
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Who am I (teacher)?
GET {{base}}/users/me/
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### TEACHER — slot CRUD
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

### Create a slot (teacher) — change the dates to be in the future!
# @name newSlot
POST {{base}}/teacher/slots/
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "start_time": "2026-05-10T18:00:00Z",
  "end_time":   "2026-05-10T19:00:00Z"
}

### Capture the slot id for later requests
@slotId = {{newSlot.response.body.id}}

### List teacher's own slots
GET {{base}}/teacher/slots/
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}

### Edit the slot (only allowed while is_booked = false)
PATCH {{base}}/teacher/slots/{{slotId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "end_time": "2026-05-10T19:30:00Z"
}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### STUDENT — see open slots, then book one
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

### Student lists open slots
GET {{base}}/slots/
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Student books the slot we just created
# @name booking
POST {{base}}/lessons/
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slot": {{slotId}}
}

### Capture the lesson id for the rest of the flow
@lessonId = {{booking.response.body.id}}

### Student lists their lessons (should show 1 PENDING)
GET {{base}}/lessons/
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### TEACHER — confirm the booking (queues Celery reminders)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

### Confirm — watch your Celery terminal: it should log task scheduling
POST {{base}}/lessons/{{lessonId}}/confirm/
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}

### Teacher lists their lessons (should show 1 CONFIRMED)
GET {{base}}/lessons/
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### TEACHER — write the post-lesson report → lesson becomes COMPLETED
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

POST {{base}}/reports/
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lesson": {{lessonId}},
  "topic": "Past Simple",
  "text":  "Good progress on regular verbs. Practice irregular ones for next time."
}

### Verify student's stats updated (total_lessons + streak should be 1, rank "Starter")
GET {{base}}/users/me/
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### STUDENT — leave a review
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

POST {{base}}/reviews/
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lesson": {{lessonId}},
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "Great lesson, very clear explanations."
}

### Read your own reviews
GET {{base}}/reviews/
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### EDGE CASES — these should FAIL with a sensible error
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

### Try to book the same slot again — expect 400 "already booked"
POST {{base}}/lessons/
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slot": {{slotId}}
}

### Try to confirm with student token — expect 403
POST {{base}}/lessons/{{lessonId}}/confirm/
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Try to write a second report — expect 400 "report already exists"
POST {{base}}/reports/
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lesson": {{lessonId}},
  "topic": "Duplicate",
  "text": "should fail"
}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### CANCELLATION — create a *new* slot/lesson, then cancel it
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

### Teacher creates a slot far in the future (free cancellation)
# @name slotForCancel
POST {{base}}/teacher/slots/
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "start_time": "2026-12-20T18:00:00Z",
  "end_time":   "2026-12-20T19:00:00Z"
}

@slotForCancelId = {{slotForCancel.response.body.id}}

### Student books it
# @name lessonForCancel
POST {{base}}/lessons/
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slot": {{slotForCancelId}}
}

@lessonForCancelId = {{lessonForCancel.response.body.id}}

### Cancel — far in the future, so cancellation_charged should be false
POST {{base}}/lessons/{{lessonForCancelId}}/cancel/
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Verify the slot is back on the open list
GET {{base}}/slots/
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
